        .thenAccept(System.out::println);
Characteristics

✅ Supports task chaining
✅ Combine multiple async calls
✅ Exception handling
⚠️ Still uses thread-based model

Best Use Cases

Parallel API calls

Microservice aggregation

Complex async workflows

3️⃣ Reactive Programming (WebFlux / Reactor)

Reactive programming uses event-driven, non-blocking streams instead of threads.

In Spring reactive systems this is usually done with Project Reactor.

Example:

Mono<User> user = userService.getUser();
user.flatMap(u -> orderService.getOrders(u))
    .subscribe(System.out::println);
Characteristics

✅ Non-blocking architecture
✅ Handles very high concurrency
✅ Uses event loop instead of threads

Best Use Cases

High-traffic APIs

Streaming systems

Real-time applications

